# {{PROJECT_SLUG}}-context

Knowledge base and Claude Code marketplace of the **{{PROJECT_NAME}}** project — the
single source of its project knowledge: nothing about scope, decisions, vocabulary or
ownership is authoritative anywhere else. Start at [docs/README.md](docs/README.md). Why
it exists and how to use it: [GUIDE.md](GUIDE.md).

## Rules

1. **State of today.** A living document describes only the currently accepted state.
   History lives in version control and in decision records. Two live documents never
   contradict; [docs/decisions/](docs/decisions/README.md) is the tie-breaker.
2. **Decisions live in one place — this repository.** Every record is a file in
   [docs/decisions/](docs/decisions/README.md), indexed there with a `Scope` column,
   **never in a code repository**. **Only `Accepted` binds.** Write one with
   `/tsh-core:managing-decision-records`, pointing it at `docs/decisions/` as the
   archive; that skill owns the format, the statuses and the index schema, and
   [conventions/decisions.md](conventions/decisions.md) matches them. This holds from
   every repository of the project: a decision discussed in a code repository is still
   written here.
3. **One space, one owner.** Every workspace under `docs/` has a `CLAUDE.md` naming its
   owner; read it before editing there, and the owner reviews the change. Standard:
   [conventions/ownership.md](conventions/ownership.md).
4. **Only project-specific instructions in `plugins/`, Markdown only.** A skill or agent
   lands in `plugins/{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-shared/` only when it is specific to this project
   and more than one role or repository needs it — and never a hook, MCP server or
   script: the whole team installs this plugin. Every change to it bumps `version`.
   Rule: [plugins/{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-shared/README.md](plugins/{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-shared/README.md).
5. **Every change goes through a branch and a pull request.** Nothing is pushed to the
   default branch directly; the owner of the area reviews. The skills below write on
   their own branch and push only after you say yes.

## Quality gate

Every relative link must resolve and every markdown filename must be kebab-case; every
markdown table must render; decision numbers must be unique; the plugin must stay
Markdown-only and versioned. Checked by:

```shell
python3 scripts/check_links.py
python3 scripts/check_tables.py
python3 scripts/check_decisions.py
python3 scripts/check_plugin.py --base origin/<default branch>
```

`bitbucket-pipelines.yml` runs all four on every pull request; on another git host, run
them in its pipeline. Protect the default branch on the host (no direct pushes, one
approval) — that, not a script, is what guarantees nothing lands unreviewed. Table defects in particular fail silently —
the table renders, just wrongly — and these documents get exported for people outside
the team. With the shared plugin installed,
`/tsh-product-management:repairing-project-context-links` runs both and repairs what it finds.

## Working here

| I want to… | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Read what the project has decided or defined | `/tsh-product-management:navigating-project-context` |
| Add or update a document | `/tsh-product-management:writing-project-knowledge` |
| Create a new workspace | `/tsh-product-management:adding-project-context-workspace` |
| Fix broken links or tables | `/tsh-product-management:repairing-project-context-links` |
| Record a decision | `/tsh-core:managing-decision-records`, targeting `docs/decisions/` in this repository |

## Keeping this current

When structure or conventions change, update the affected file in the same change.
With `tsh-core` installed, `/tsh-core:managing-claude-context` owns this file and the
workspace `CLAUDE.md` files; without it, revise by hand and keep this file short.
